Z||000013||BENGAL4||12-15-1999||10:12 AM||||I personally don't own a gun, but I cherish my right to. Dogtired commented on everyone 100 years ago carried guns. Our problem started 20 to 30 years ago when parents started losing control of thier homes and teachers were stripped of thier power in the schools. I graduated 25 years ago and back then if I got in trouble at school, my dad was going to take care of it when I got home. So I didn't cause any trouble because I respected my parents and my teachers. Most kids today have respect for neither. I have friends who didn't make thier daughter obey when she was 2, now she is 17 and out of control. Forum members. love your kids and get involved in thier lives. Know who thier friends are and thier parents. I'll get off the soap box now. S  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Racer 1||12-15-1999||12:20 PM||||Im a proud member of NRA I cherish my right to keep and bear arms. I was raised around .22 gun in the house but my father took me out shooting when I was about 6 years old and taught me what a gun can do and how to be safe with them. Then around eight I got a red rider BB gun and knew saftey first. I have around 14 guns now that are locked in a gun safe. Its always easier to blame the law "abiding"&lt;--wrong spelling--citizens then to make new laws to keep bad guys in jail. Some people forgot how the country was won by armed citizens. Sorry to bore you just my opinion.||||reg||10
